From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: zero3w: USB0 is a device port, fix otg manager probe

USB0 sits on the power-in Type-C (schematic p.11: CC1/CC2 each 5.1k Rd to
GND, VBUS tied to the board 5 V rail), so it is a sink/device port and has
no ID pin (usb_id_gpio is empty). The vendor node declares it OTG with
vbus/id detection and usb_detect_mode = 2 ("pmu notify", only for
axp2202); usb_manager.c rejects that combination and the otg manager
fails to probe with -1 on every boot, leaving the dual-role/typec parts
unregistered. Declare it a device port: the manager probes, starts the
UDC once, and otg_role can still switch to usb_host when the board is fed
from the 40-pin 5 V (vendor Debian images do that at boot).

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
index d33a30b60..4bfcdb9da 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts
@@ -1667,7 +1667,14 @@ &sdc1 {
  */
 &usbc0 {
 	device_type = "usbc0";
-	usb_port_type = <0x2>;
+	/*
+	 * USB0 is the power-in Type-C (schematic p.11: CC1/CC2 5.1k Rd to GND,
+	 * VBUS = board VCC-5V): a device port with no ID pin. As OTG with
+	 * vbus/id detection + "pmu notify" mode (only for axp2202) the otg
+	 * manager failed to probe (-1). Start as device; otg_role still
+	 * switches to usb_host (board fed from the 40-pin 5 V).
+	 */
+	usb_port_type = <0x0>;
 // #ifdef TYPEC_DP
 // 	usb_detect_type = <0x3>;
 // #else
